// Signing for the iOS app.
//
// A team id belongs to one Apple account, so committing one would break the device
// build for everybody else. Put yours in Signing.local.xcconfig instead, which git
// ignores:
//
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID
//
// Find the id in Xcode under Settings > Accounts: pick your Apple ID and read the
// ten character id beside the team. Selecting the team in the target's
// Signing & Capabilities tab also creates the signing certificate, which does not
// exist until you do that.
//
// Every build needs a team now, the simulator too, because the team id is part of the
// bundle identifier (see AAPS_CLIENT_ID_PREFIX below). This is the way Trio does it.
// Without one the "Build shared framework" step stops with an error naming this file.
//
// The include stays optional all the same, the `?` is what makes it so. A required
// include that is missing does NOT fail the build: Xcode drops this whole file with a
// warning and carries on, which would lose the version numbers and every setting here.
//
// A simulator build gets its entitlements from Simulator.entitlements rather than
// from a profile, because the Keychain refuses to work without them. That file says
// why.
//
// This file itself must stay committed. Xcode treats a missing base configuration
// as an error, not a warning, so pointing the project straight at an ignored file
// would break every fresh clone.
// The start of the clients' bundle identifiers. Somebody who builds a client themselves
// gets their own team id in it - app.aaps.<teamid>.client and app.aaps.<teamid>.client2 -
// which keeps every builder's app apart and lets Xcode register the App ID by itself.
//
// app.aaps.client and app.aaps.client2 are the project's own published apps in App Store
// Connect. A build that publishes them puts this line in Signing.local.xcconfig, as
// .github/workflows/ios-testflight.yml does:
//
//     AAPS_CLIENT_ID_PREFIX = app.aaps
//
// The full app has no such switch. It is always app.aaps.<teamid>.full, set on the target.
// Set before the include so that the local file can override it.
AAPS_CLIENT_ID_PREFIX = app.aaps.$(DEVELOPMENT_TEAM)

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"

// The generated version numbers, from :ios:shell:generateIosVersionXcconfig. Optional for the same
// reason as the file above: a clone that has never run Gradle still builds, using the project's own
// MARKETING_VERSION and CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION. Only an upload to App Store Connect needs real
// ones, because it rejects a build number it has already seen.
#include? "Version.xcconfig"
